# DDD architecture

## Bounded contexts

- **catalog** — the Scryfall mirror. `Card`, `Printing`; `ScryfallId`, `OracleId`, `SetCode`, `CollectorNumber`.
- **resolution** — spoken string to ranked candidates. A **pure domain service**: no I/O, catalog behind a port.
- **collection** — the core domain. `Collection` aggregate over `CollectionEntry`; `Quantity`, `Finish`, `Condition`, `Language`; domain events.
- **voice** — `VoiceSession` over `Utterance`. Holds pending/unconfirmed state.
- **sync** — distribution. `CollectionTargetPort` plus one anti-corruption adapter per platform.

## Layering is uneven on purpose

| Context | Layers |
|---|---|
| resolution, collection | `domain` / `application` / `infrastructure` |
| catalog, voice, sync | `domain` / `infrastructure` |

Do **not** add an `application` layer to catalog, voice, or sync speculatively. Promote one when a real use case needs orchestrating, and say what it buys per `feedback-and-justification.mdc`.

## The dependency rule

`domain` depends on nothing. `application` depends only on `domain`. `infrastructure` implements ports declared in `domain`.

- Ports (interfaces) live in `domain/`, adapters in `infrastructure/`.
- Never `new` an infrastructure class inside `domain/` or `application/`. Constructor-inject the port.
- No Zod, HTTP, SQL, or vendor SDK imports anywhere under `domain/`.

## Value objects over primitives

A Scryfall ID is not a `string`. Wrap identifiers and quantities so they cannot be swapped by accident.

```ts
// BAD — these are trivially transposable
function addCard(scryfallId: string, setCode: string, quantity: number)

// GOOD
function addCard(options: { scryfallId: ScryfallId; setCode: SetCode; quantity: Quantity })
```

## Domain events over in-place mutation

State changes on `Collection` emit events (`CardAdded`, `CardRemoved`, `QuantityChanged`, `EntryCorrected`) appended to the log. Corrections are compensating events, never updates.
